# Trackless Web SDK — AI Integration Rules

This package is `@trackless-telemetry/sdk-web`, a privacy-first web analytics SDK. See GUIDE.md in this directory for the complete integration guide.

## Quick Reference

1. Install: `npm install @trackless-telemetry/sdk-web`
2. Configure once at app startup with just an API key:
   ```typescript
   import { Trackless } from "@trackless-telemetry/sdk-web";
   Trackless.configure({ apiKey: "tl_your_api_key_here" });
   ```
3. Call typed event methods anywhere:
   - `Trackless.view("home")` — page/screen views (optional detail: `Trackless.view("home", "pricing")`)
   - `Trackless.feature("export", "csv")` — feature usage; name the feature, put the variant in the optional detail
   - `Trackless.funnel("checkout", 0, "view_cart")` — multi-step flows
   - `Trackless.performance("api_fetch", 0.342)` — durationSeconds in seconds (optional thresholdSeconds: `Trackless.performance("api_fetch", 0.342, 2.0)`)
   - `Trackless.error("payment_failed", "DECLINED")` — something went wrong; counts toward errors per session and every alert
   - `Trackless.info("tier", "paid")` — something worth counting that the user did not do and that did not go wrong; never counts toward errors or alerts

## Important Rules

- Do NOT create a wrapper hook or service (`useAnalytics()`, `analytics.ts`, `TrackingService`) — `Trackless` is already a static singleton; import it and call it directly
- `detail` is a SEPARATE argument, never concatenated into the name: `Trackless.feature("export", "csv")`, not `Trackless.feature("export_csv")` — the dashboard groups detail distributions per name
- Two levels only: `error(name, code?)` for what went wrong, `info(name, detail?)` for what did not. Call `info()` once per session for a property you want a session split on (`Trackless.info("tier", isPaid ? "paid" : "free")`) — it counts sessions, not people. Report configuration many sessions share, never anything about the person. Never share a name between `error()` and `info()`
- The `severity` parameter on `error()` is deprecated but still compiles: `"error" | "warning" | "fatal"` are sent as `error`, `"info" | "debug"` as `info`
- The endpoint defaults to `https://api.tracklesstelemetry.com` — do NOT require the user to provide it
- Store the API key in an environment variable (e.g., `VITE_TRACKLESS_API_KEY`), never hardcode in committed source
- Event names and fields (`detail`, `step`, `code`) are auto-normalized: lowercased, spaces/special chars replaced with `_`, trimmed, truncated to 100 chars. Developers can pass natural strings like `"Sign Up Button"` (becomes `"sign_up_button"`). Use the optional `detail` parameter on `feature()` and `view()` to distinguish variants — dashboard auto-groups features with detail values into donut charts
- Performance duration is in **seconds**, not milliseconds
- `environment` defaults to `"sandbox"` only on localhost / `*.localhost` / `127.x.x.x` / `[::1]` / `0.0.0.0`, and to `"production"` everywhere else; an explicit value always wins. Set it explicitly for LAN IPs, `.local`/`.test` hosts, staging, preview deploys and Electron / `file:` pages
- The SDK sends no distribution channel and never sends the page hostname — do NOT add one
- Entry-point `configure()` (main.ts) needs no `destroy()`; call `Trackless.destroy()` only in effect-mounted setups (e.g., Next.js app-router useEffect cleanup)
- Zero client persistence: no cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage, or IndexedDB
- PII patterns (emails, phone numbers, SSNs) are automatically stripped from all event fields before buffering
- Sessions are managed automatically — no manual session handling needed
- For SPA route tracking, use `autoScreenTracking: true` or integrate with your router
